{"user": "okay, what other advice can i get for the next game", "user_ts": "2026-08-18T21:30:56.759198+00:00", "assistant": "For next game, focus on these habits:\n\n1. **Don\u2019t chase big flips early.** Big flips often give your opponent more moves and targets.\n\n2. **Corners are gold.** A corner can never be flipped. Try to take them, but more importantly: don\u2019t give them away.\n\n3. **Be careful with X-squares and C-squares.**\n   - X-squares: **b2, g2, b7, g7** \u2014 diagonal to corners.\n   - C-squares: **a2, b1, g1, h2, a7, b8, g8, h7** \u2014 next to corners.\n   Playing these too early often hands over a corner.\n\n4. **Think mobility.** Ask: \u201cAfter I move, how many legal moves will White have?\u201d Fewer White moves is usually good.\n\n5. **Stable discs matter more than many discs.** Edge discs connected to corners are strong; center discs can flip back and forth.\n\n6. **In the endgame, count.** Don\u2019t ask \u201cwhat flips most now?\u201d Ask \u201cwhat final count does this line lead to?\u201d", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-18T21:30:57.610521+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-18T21:31:01.965058+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Solution Request"], "votes": {"Conversational Acknowledgment": 3, "Solution Request": 3}, "confidence": {"Conversational Acknowledgment": 1.0, "Solution Request": 1.0}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Solution Request"], "gpt": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Solution Request"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle"], "llama": ["General Pr